go 1.24

// The repository root is deliberately NOT a module. Only this file lives here,
// so a go.mod and a go.work never sit side by side confusing which one governs.
//
// Every module's directory equals its import path suffix, which Go requires:
// a module declaring github.com/ubgo/lath/kit MUST sit at kit/, or the
// proxy cannot resolve it. An earlier layout kept these under modules/ and was
// unfetchable by anyone outside this checkout — it worked only because replace
// directives and this file hid the mismatch.
//
//	cmd/lath   github.com/ubgo/lath/cmd/lath   the runner; links nothing of ours
//	kit        github.com/ubgo/lath/kit        libraries, no lath dependency
//	pipeline   github.com/ubgo/lath/pipeline   the Step contract, no dependency
//	steps      github.com/ubgo/lath/steps      adapters: kit + pipeline
//
// example/ is a stand-in for a USER's repository: lath is a dependency of its
// definition, not a sibling of its application.
//
// example/.lath is deliberately ABSENT. It is a nested module that must stay
// outside the workspace so `go work vendor` and `go build ./...` never reach
// it. That exclusion is the mechanism under test — run `task isolation`.
use (
	./cmd/lath
	./kit
	./pipeline
	./steps
	./example
)
